Subject: Cache the global-variable property slot, not its offset

What this does
  Cache the global-variable property slot, not its offset.

Why we need it
  Which is what kept `meth` and `m0` behind.

What it adds
  `JSGVCell` caches the `JSProperty *` itself, so the hit path is generation + atom + slot + value; the generation must be bumped wherever a watched object's property array can move, so the two add-transition IC replays (`regvm_put_field_add_hit` and the stack VM's) now invalidate a watched receiver like the generic add paths already did; every other mover (`resize_properties`, `compact_properties`, `add_property`, the in-place shape mutations, the TDZ write) was already behind an invalidate.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
